[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
=====================================================================
PhoenixAdult has been installed.

1. Configure it. Copy the sample env and edit it:

     # cp %%DATADIR%%/env.sample %%PA_DIR%%/.env
     # chown %%PA_USER%%:%%PA_GROUP%% %%PA_DIR%%/.env

2. Enable and start the service:

     # sysrc phoenixadult_enable=YES
     # service phoenixadult start

   Then browse to http://<host>:3000/config for the web UI.
   Logs: %%PA_DIR%%/logs/agent.log

The optional feature extras (face cropping = opencv, the Impersonate
bypass = curl_cffi, Playwright) depend on packages that are not in the
ports tree; they stay disabled. To use them, install those packages
into a virtualenv yourself -- the features no-op gracefully when absent.

Uninstalling leaves %%PA_DIR%% (config + caches) and the "%%PA_USER%%"
account in place. Remove them by hand if you no longer need the data.
=====================================================================
EOM
}
]
